1
00:00:12,923 --> 00:00:15,056
(This program contains indirect advertisements.)

2
00:00:15,137 --> 00:00:16,777
(Autumn is just around the corner.)

3
00:00:16,777 --> 00:00:18,037
Hello.

4
00:00:18,037 --> 00:00:19,877
- Hello, CEO Song.
- Hello, my friend.

5
00:00:20,277 --> 00:00:22,147
Shall we hurry up and order our drinks?

6
00:00:22,147 --> 00:00:23,677
- I already ordered mine.
- I ordered a chocolate latte.

7
00:00:23,677 --> 00:00:26,317
- We got ready quite early.
- Right.

8
00:00:26,497 --> 00:00:29,267
We got here way earlier than the production crew expected.

9
00:00:29,737 --> 00:00:32,807
Why did everyone get here so early?

10
00:00:32,937 --> 00:00:34,907
I got here early too,

11
00:00:34,907 --> 00:00:37,307
so I was just resting in my car nearby.

12
00:00:37,607 --> 00:00:39,547
- Then my manager woke me up.
- Why?

13
00:00:40,317 --> 00:00:41,447
He said your car had driven past.

14
00:00:42,647 --> 00:00:43,687
(Then you should hurry.)

15
00:00:43,687 --> 00:00:46,517
What does that have to do with anything?

16
00:00:46,517 --> 00:00:49,087
- He didn't want us to be late.
- I see.

17
00:00:49,317 --> 00:00:52,387
My manager never wants to get here late.

18
00:00:52,387 --> 00:00:55,557
Every time, we've been getting here exactly on time.

19
00:00:55,557 --> 00:00:57,867
But today, we wanted to get here early.

20
00:00:57,867 --> 00:01:01,097
No matter how early we are...

21
00:01:01,097 --> 00:01:03,167
(1 person who's always here 1st)

22
00:01:05,007 --> 00:01:06,307
I can't get here earlier than him.

23
00:01:06,307 --> 00:01:07,437
That's strange.

24
00:01:07,637 --> 00:01:10,677
Kyoung Pyo got his hair curled.

25
00:01:10,677 --> 00:01:11,877
Yes, today...

26
00:01:12,247 --> 00:01:14,217
- It's starting to feel like autumn.
- Right.

27
00:01:14,217 --> 00:01:15,947
- So I changed my hairstyle.
- Right.

28
00:01:15,947 --> 00:01:17,317
Yes, he looks handsome.

29
00:01:17,847 --> 00:01:21,717
He looks like an uncle who's been cooped up all summer...

30
00:01:21,957 --> 00:01:23,657
and finally got a makeover...

31
00:01:23,657 --> 00:01:25,787
- for autumn.
- Right.

32
00:01:26,527 --> 00:01:28,657
To start dating.

33
00:01:29,967 --> 00:01:32,227
I hope today's guest will be someone beautiful.

34
00:01:32,227 --> 00:01:33,737
(Getting ready for a date, before and after)

35
00:01:33,937 --> 00:01:36,097
(While they're chatting, today's guests have arrived.)

36
00:01:36,097 --> 00:01:37,137
Hello.

37
00:01:37,437 --> 00:01:38,867
(Guests with a solid build appear.)

38
00:01:38,867 --> 00:01:40,307
Hello.

39
00:01:40,537 --> 00:01:41,977
- They're here.
- Who are they?

40
00:01:41,977 --> 00:01:43,377
(They greet them with excitement. Who are the guests?)

41
00:01:43,377 --> 00:01:45,507
- Oh, my.
- It's Han Sang Jin.

42
00:01:45,507 --> 00:01:47,717
- Goodness, hello.
- Gosh.

43
00:01:48,817 --> 00:01:50,247
- Welcome.
- Hello.

44
00:01:50,247 --> 00:01:51,717
Hi.

45
00:01:51,947 --> 00:01:53,017
Hi.

46
00:01:53,017 --> 00:01:55,857
- Long time, no see, Heo Sung Tae.
- Hello.

47
00:01:56,217 --> 00:01:59,887
(From chilling villains...)

48
00:02:00,327 --> 00:02:03,157
(to hilarious comedic roles)

49
00:02:03,527 --> 00:02:06,997
(The incredibly versatile actor, Heo Sung Tae)

50
00:02:07,397 --> 00:02:10,867
(A veteran actor with 29 years of experience)

51
00:02:11,037 --> 00:02:13,167
(Why do you keep using this emoticon at the end?)

52
00:02:13,167 --> 00:02:14,177
(So that you wrap it up)

53
00:02:14,507 --> 00:02:16,847
(Jae Seok's signature emoticon, wrap it up)

54
00:02:16,907 --> 00:02:20,677
(A natural-born entertainer loved for his unstoppable gift of gab)

55
00:02:20,977 --> 00:02:24,187
(Today's guests, Heo Sung Tae, Han Sang Jin)

56
00:02:24,447 --> 00:02:26,287
- Sung Tae and Sang Jin are...
- I'm glad to see you both.

57
00:02:26,287 --> 00:02:28,387
- from the same agency.
- Right now?

58
00:02:28,717 --> 00:02:31,887
(Agency colleagues making a variety show appearance together)

59
00:02:32,087 --> 00:02:35,627
I recently saw Sung Tae on another show.

60
00:02:35,997 --> 00:02:38,427
Why do you look so grumpy today?

61
00:02:38,427 --> 00:02:39,567
Is it because you came here with Sang Jin?

62
00:02:39,567 --> 00:02:41,667
(Me?)

63
00:02:42,167 --> 00:02:43,267
Hello.

64
00:02:43,267 --> 00:02:44,267
(Unbelievable)

65
00:02:44,267 --> 00:02:46,067
(Actually, the two are close friends.)

66
00:02:46,207 --> 00:02:47,977
(What's with the role-playing already?)

67
00:02:47,977 --> 00:02:49,707
We need to make things clear.

68
00:02:49,707 --> 00:02:51,407
I felt like I had to drive for him.

69
00:02:51,407 --> 00:02:53,177
We're short on managers these days.

70
00:02:53,417 --> 00:02:54,647
How many staff members did you bring today?

71
00:02:55,477 --> 00:02:56,917
Don't ask me that.

72
00:02:57,747 --> 00:02:59,117
He's sensitive about...

73
00:02:59,117 --> 00:03:00,517
- the number of staff members.
- Really?

74
00:03:00,517 --> 00:03:02,357
I joined the agency first,

75
00:03:02,357 --> 00:03:03,927
but he gets 4 or 5 people assigned to him.

76
00:03:03,927 --> 00:03:05,387
And I always get one person.

77
00:03:05,927 --> 00:03:07,927
(It's a sore spot for him.)

78
00:03:08,027 --> 00:03:10,097
At least you got one person.

79
00:03:10,767 --> 00:03:13,097
It's better than being told to go alone after receiving car keys.

80
00:03:13,097 --> 00:03:15,197
(Maximum damage)

81
00:03:15,567 --> 00:03:16,567
That's better, isn't it?

82
00:03:16,567 --> 00:03:18,437
- Is having a big staff important?
- What?

83
00:03:18,437 --> 00:03:20,077
- Is having a big staff important?
- It's just...

84
00:03:20,077 --> 00:03:21,877
- He feels...
- Is it just for show?

85
00:03:22,407 --> 00:03:24,347
- When you have...
- Right.

86
00:03:24,347 --> 00:03:25,747
- an inferiority complex, - I see.

87
00:03:25,747 --> 00:03:27,347
you notice things like that.

88
00:03:27,347 --> 00:03:28,447
(He admits to his inferiority complex.)

89
00:03:28,517 --> 00:03:30,247
(I understand.)

90
00:03:30,447 --> 00:03:32,617
Every time I see him, he asks how many staff members I brought.

91
00:03:32,617 --> 00:03:35,317
I also check. I call the head of the agency to find out.

92
00:03:35,957 --> 00:03:37,457
- He's a good guy.
- Isn't he from Busan?

93
00:03:37,457 --> 00:03:39,287
- I'm from Busan.
- Don't you live in Busan?

94
00:03:39,487 --> 00:03:41,657
He's also working hard to boost Busan's economy.

95
00:03:41,657 --> 00:03:42,957
Aren't you also from Busan?

96
00:03:43,027 --> 00:03:45,597
He's from Busan, but not really.

97
00:03:45,597 --> 00:03:46,867
I actually live in Busan.

98
00:03:46,867 --> 00:03:48,897
- That makes a difference?
- Yes.

99
00:03:49,097 --> 00:03:50,807
I'm a promotional ambassador for Busan.

100
00:03:50,807 --> 00:03:52,367
(His bragging mode is on.)

101
00:03:52,567 --> 00:03:54,107
Oh, really?

102
00:03:54,107 --> 00:03:56,847
Park Jung Eun is the head coach of Busan BNK.

103
00:03:56,847 --> 00:03:59,047
- The basketball team.
- I know.

104
00:03:59,247 --> 00:04:01,817
He's definitely riding on the coach's fame.

105
00:04:02,577 --> 00:04:04,587
You're really reaping the benefits.

106
00:04:04,587 --> 00:04:07,187
It's basically a case of ruling through a puppet ruler.

107
00:04:07,187 --> 00:04:08,187
(Coach Park's puppet)

108
00:04:08,187 --> 00:04:09,757
- Behind the scenes, - Behind the scenes...

109
00:04:09,757 --> 00:04:11,127
Coach Park is the one controlling.

110
00:04:11,127 --> 00:04:12,757
Coach Park is the one pulling all the strings.

111
00:04:12,757 --> 00:04:14,397
"You should go on Sixth Sense."

112
00:04:14,397 --> 00:04:15,927
(A secret order from Coach Park)

113
00:04:16,127 --> 00:04:18,427
My wife orders me to go on Sixth Sense?

114
00:04:18,427 --> 00:04:19,497
Seriously.

115
00:04:19,667 --> 00:04:21,037
He's doing two local TV shows...

116
00:04:21,037 --> 00:04:22,637
- in Busan.
- Really?

117
00:04:22,637 --> 00:04:23,907
Now it's gone up to four.

118
00:04:23,907 --> 00:04:25,007
Four?

119
00:04:25,507 --> 00:04:26,567
(That's impressive.)

120
00:04:26,567 --> 00:04:28,107
Really? That's amazing.

121
00:04:28,737 --> 00:04:29,807
Do they only air in Busan?

122
00:04:30,037 --> 00:04:31,577
No.

123
00:04:31,777 --> 00:04:34,477
Jae Seok said that they were local shows.

124
00:04:34,477 --> 00:04:35,547
It's not what I meant.

125
00:04:35,877 --> 00:04:38,117
- Wait, did you clench your fist?
- It's not what I meant.

126
00:04:38,117 --> 00:04:39,587
(Please help.)

127
00:04:39,747 --> 00:04:41,787
There's no need to get defensive.

128
00:04:42,257 --> 00:04:43,457
(His feelings are hurt as much as he is proud.)

129
00:04:43,457 --> 00:04:45,057
- He has an inferiority complex.
- Please don't misunderstand.

130
00:04:45,057 --> 00:04:46,357
- There's no need to get defensive.
- He has an inferiority complex.

131
00:04:46,357 --> 00:04:47,427
I can't say anything freely.

132
00:04:47,427 --> 00:04:48,597
Since you keep getting worked up,

133
00:04:48,597 --> 00:04:50,327
you end up getting cupping therapy on your back.

134
00:04:50,667 --> 00:04:52,927
He bent over, and there was a cupping mark this big.

135
00:04:53,067 --> 00:04:56,337
As I get older, my blood pressure suddenly shoots up.

136
00:04:56,337 --> 00:04:59,467
- So I have to get cupping therapy.
- But he's a good guy.

137
00:05:01,737 --> 00:05:04,147
- The drinks are here.
- What's that?

138
00:05:04,147 --> 00:05:06,077
- Thank you.
- Who ordered a latte?

139
00:05:06,077 --> 00:05:07,077
(The drinks arrive.)

140
00:05:07,577 --> 00:05:08,677
I need some wet tissue.

141
00:05:09,517 --> 00:05:11,887
Jae Seok got something on his hand. Hurry...

142
00:05:12,087 --> 00:05:13,957
Jae Seok got something on his hand.

143
00:05:13,957 --> 00:05:15,587
Hurry and bring some wet tissue.

144
00:05:15,887 --> 00:05:17,287
Jae Seok got something on his hand.

145
00:05:17,287 --> 00:05:18,627
(Laughing)

146
00:05:18,887 --> 00:05:21,227
- You guys are too loud.
- I was quicker than you.

147
00:05:22,027 --> 00:05:23,827
Gosh, you're making such a fuss.

148
00:05:24,567 --> 00:05:26,467
Why did both of you go to get some napkin?

149
00:05:26,467 --> 00:05:27,697
Eun I doesn't like it when it's loud.

150
00:05:27,697 --> 00:05:28,937
If you're going to be quiet on a variety show,

151
00:05:28,937 --> 00:05:30,137
you might as well do radio.

152
00:05:30,307 --> 00:05:31,567
(Laughing)

153
00:05:31,707 --> 00:05:33,267
Did you hear my inner thoughts?

154
00:05:33,267 --> 00:05:35,007
- That was too obvious.
- I'm sorry.

155
00:05:35,837 --> 00:05:39,177
Have you ever worked with BIBI? Maybe on a show?

156
00:05:39,607 --> 00:05:40,847
This is my first time meeting them.

157
00:05:40,847 --> 00:05:42,647
- It's our first time.
- We never worked together.

158
00:05:42,817 --> 00:05:44,547
"Yeon Yang..."

159
00:05:45,117 --> 00:05:46,117
- "Yang..." - "Bam..."

160
00:05:46,317 --> 00:05:49,617
(What? What is he saying?)

161
00:05:49,787 --> 00:05:51,257
"Bam Yang Gang." It's not Yeon Yang Gang.

162
00:05:51,257 --> 00:05:52,857
"Yeon Yang Gang?" Come on.

163
00:05:53,457 --> 00:05:55,357
- "Yeon Yang Gang" sounds good too.
- "Yeon Yang Gang."

164
00:05:55,597 --> 00:05:57,127
"Yeon Yang Gang?"

165
00:05:57,627 --> 00:05:59,097
That's really shocking.

166
00:05:59,097 --> 00:06:00,267
Healthy and delicious

167
00:06:00,267 --> 00:06:01,437
- Yeon Yang Gang - Yeon Yang Gang

168
00:06:01,437 --> 00:06:02,997
(Healthy and delicious Yeon Yang Gang)

169
00:06:02,997 --> 00:06:05,667
(Even the original singer approves.)

170
00:06:05,907 --> 00:06:07,477
- Today's theme is...
- What is the theme?

171
00:06:07,477 --> 00:06:09,577
"We actually make a pretty good pair."

172
00:06:09,577 --> 00:06:12,677
(We actually make a pretty good pair)

173
00:06:12,807 --> 00:06:14,577
Is that why we have them as guests today?

174
00:06:14,577 --> 00:06:16,677
- Is that why?
- That must be it.

175
00:06:16,747 --> 00:06:19,017
(I don't think so.)

176
00:06:19,217 --> 00:06:21,017
You make a pretty good pair but not a perfect match.

177
00:06:21,017 --> 00:06:22,117
We don't make a perfect match.

178
00:06:22,117 --> 00:06:25,257
The word "pretty" is quite important.

179
00:06:25,627 --> 00:06:26,957
That's important.

180
00:06:27,327 --> 00:06:30,767
Today, instead of using cassette tapes,

181
00:06:30,767 --> 00:06:33,197
- we're using cell phones.
- Is that so?

182
00:06:33,797 --> 00:06:35,697
This phone setup is totally new.

183
00:06:35,697 --> 00:06:36,867
The design is so pretty.

184
00:06:36,867 --> 00:06:39,167
It's a full-on flip phone, so it's easy to hold it.

185
00:06:39,167 --> 00:06:40,207
Right?

186
00:06:41,007 --> 00:06:42,437
Let's take a look at the hint.

187
00:06:42,907 --> 00:06:44,547
I love how big and clear the screen is.

188
00:06:44,547 --> 00:06:45,647
Right.

189
00:06:45,647 --> 00:06:46,807
(The hint for the first location)

190
00:06:46,807 --> 00:06:48,117
Why isn't this included?

191
00:06:48,317 --> 00:06:49,747
Aren't you supposed to mix them?

192
00:06:50,147 --> 00:06:51,987
It's like Indian meets Korean, right?

193
00:06:52,087 --> 00:06:53,687
"Aren't you supposed to mix them?"

194
00:06:53,687 --> 00:06:54,787
"It's like..."

195
00:06:54,787 --> 00:06:56,287
- "Indian meets Korean, right?" - "Indian meets Korean, right?"

196
00:06:57,727 --> 00:06:58,757
Could it be curry?

197
00:06:58,757 --> 00:07:01,097
(When you think of India, curry naturally comes to mind.)

198
00:07:01,497 --> 00:07:03,567
Could it be a fusion dish today?

199
00:07:03,567 --> 00:07:05,927
- Maybe that's it.
- You're supposed to mix them.

200
00:07:05,927 --> 00:07:07,437
Why isn't this included?

201
00:07:08,497 --> 00:07:09,597
It's the second location.

202
00:07:09,937 --> 00:07:10,967
This is it.

203
00:07:10,967 --> 00:07:12,407
(The second restaurant's clue is a video of customer reviews.)

204
00:07:12,467 --> 00:07:14,577
- A short-form video came up.
- Right?

205
00:07:14,677 --> 00:07:16,407
- The short-form video is big.
- Yes.

206
00:07:17,107 --> 00:07:18,647
Today, we're visiting a place we've been looking forward to...

207
00:07:18,647 --> 00:07:20,177
for a long time.

208
00:07:20,417 --> 00:07:23,847
Here, the shaman reads your fortune up to...

209
00:07:24,047 --> 00:07:25,487
Gosh, they're spot-on.

210
00:07:25,747 --> 00:07:27,557
- The talismans are works of art.
- "Talismans?"

211
00:07:27,787 --> 00:07:29,757
- It was such a fascinating place.
- Talismans?

212
00:07:30,217 --> 00:07:32,027
I'd come back 1,000 percent!

213
00:07:32,327 --> 00:07:34,157
The second place is somewhere they write talismans for you.

214
00:07:34,157 --> 00:07:35,727
She also mentioned a shaman.

215
00:07:35,727 --> 00:07:37,197
There was something about them...

216
00:07:37,197 --> 00:07:38,597
- reading your something.
- Exactly.

217
00:07:39,167 --> 00:07:40,837
- Fortune?
- Maybe they serve you...

218
00:07:40,837 --> 00:07:43,397
food based on your fortune.

219
00:07:43,397 --> 00:07:44,907
Food that matches...

220
00:07:45,807 --> 00:07:47,677
- your fortune for the day.
- Food that's right for you?

221
00:07:47,677 --> 00:07:49,507
"Eat this food because it's meant for you."

222
00:07:49,677 --> 00:07:50,807
I don't think so.

223
00:07:50,877 --> 00:07:52,307
(Pouting)

224
00:07:52,347 --> 00:07:53,477
We did that last season.

225
00:07:54,117 --> 00:07:55,617
They did it last season.

226
00:07:55,817 --> 00:07:57,247
- I got confused.
- You never watched our show.

227
00:07:57,247 --> 00:07:58,687
(Embarrassed)

228
00:07:59,117 --> 00:08:01,217
(He got caught.)

229
00:08:01,487 --> 00:08:05,527
(What could be this fortune-telling place?)

230
00:08:05,787 --> 00:08:07,757
- It's really nice.
- The third hint is a blog post.

231
00:08:08,227 --> 00:08:09,497
Let's see what it says.

232
00:08:09,657 --> 00:08:10,997
- It's nice that we can zoom in...
- The text is huge.

233
00:08:10,997 --> 00:08:12,327
- on the text.
- Yes.

234
00:08:12,327 --> 00:08:13,597
- Right.
- It's very nice.

235
00:08:13,967 --> 00:08:15,467
"I happened to stop by this place for a meal,"

236
00:08:15,467 --> 00:08:16,937
"and it was amazing."

237
00:08:17,437 --> 00:08:19,007
"Even the tableware and water glasses impressed me."

238
00:08:19,007 --> 00:08:20,737
"I highly recommend that you visit."

239
00:08:21,007 --> 00:08:23,307
"As I was busy eating, a thought suddenly crossed my mind."

240
00:08:23,307 --> 00:08:25,047
"Italians would faint if they saw this."

241
00:08:25,047 --> 00:08:27,817
(The hint for the third location)

242
00:08:28,117 --> 00:08:31,487
(A dish that would make Italians faint?)

243
00:08:32,687 --> 00:08:34,587
It must be related to Italy.

244
00:08:35,617 --> 00:08:38,387
There are a few things that would make Italians faint.

245
00:08:39,027 --> 00:08:40,027
Right, that pizza.

246
00:08:40,027 --> 00:08:41,327
(Pineapple pizza that Italians hate?)

247
00:08:42,157 --> 00:08:43,927
- Pasta.
- Breaking spaghetti in half.

248
00:08:44,627 --> 00:08:46,897
There must be another reason they would faint.

249
00:08:46,897 --> 00:08:48,637
(What does the third place serve to make Italians faint?)

250
00:08:48,737 --> 00:08:50,337
What could it be? I can't imagine it.

251
00:08:50,337 --> 00:08:52,037
We'll have to go there to find out.

252
00:08:53,007 --> 00:08:55,107
- Shall we get going?
- Gosh, it's cold.

253
00:08:56,377 --> 00:08:58,147
I love weather like this.

254
00:08:58,647 --> 00:09:00,307
I haven't tasted the flavour of Seoul in a while.

255
00:09:00,877 --> 00:09:02,717
I can smell the essence of Seoul.

256
00:09:03,577 --> 00:09:05,287
Flavours of Seoul and essence of Seoul.

257
00:09:06,347 --> 00:09:08,757
- Did you get here yesterday?
- Yes, I had a shoot yesterday.

258
00:09:08,757 --> 00:09:09,857
- Really?
- Yes.

259
00:09:09,857 --> 00:09:11,187
