- Tomorrow...

260
00:09:11,187 --> 00:09:14,297
I actually got a CT scan yesterday.

261
00:09:14,357 --> 00:09:16,057
(Why is that actually true?)

262
00:09:16,057 --> 00:09:19,097
I had a CT scan of my neck yesterday.

263
00:09:19,227 --> 00:09:20,667
Jae Seok keeps doing this...

264
00:09:20,667 --> 00:09:22,097
even though he hasn't seen me in a while.

265
00:09:22,097 --> 00:09:23,867
- Didn't I tell you?
- That's incredible.

266
00:09:24,367 --> 00:09:26,167
I actually got a CT scan.

267
00:09:26,167 --> 00:09:27,377
I had a feeling that's what...

268
00:09:27,377 --> 00:09:28,577
- the shoot was about.
- Unbelievable.

269
00:09:30,377 --> 00:09:32,247
Jae Seok knows too much about me.

270
00:09:32,247 --> 00:09:34,977
- I was spot-on, right?
- He knows me too well.

271
00:09:35,377 --> 00:09:36,747
Am I supposed to remember things like this?

272
00:09:36,747 --> 00:09:38,617
- Yes, we have to remember it.
- Remember...

273
00:09:39,017 --> 00:09:40,217
That's hilarious.

274
00:09:40,817 --> 00:09:42,687
The first restaurant is...

275
00:09:43,087 --> 00:09:45,227
- Earlier?
- It's not included.

276
00:09:45,227 --> 00:09:46,787
You're supposed to mix them.

277
00:09:47,057 --> 00:09:48,327
Indian meets Korean.

278
00:09:48,827 --> 00:09:50,467
- "Indian meets Korean." - Is it "Indian meets Korean?"

279
00:09:50,467 --> 00:09:51,567
- They meet.
- Yes.

280
00:09:51,997 --> 00:09:54,297
When it comes to India, don't we think of curry first?

281
00:09:54,297 --> 00:09:55,437
Right.

282
00:09:55,667 --> 00:09:56,737
Is this the place?

283
00:09:56,967 --> 00:09:58,767
- Is this it?
- This place?

284
00:09:58,767 --> 00:10:00,407
This is the place?

285
00:10:00,637 --> 00:10:02,177
- What?
- A sundae restaurant?

286
00:10:02,177 --> 00:10:03,807
What? A sundae restaurant?

287
00:10:04,577 --> 00:10:05,777
- This place?
- It's a sundae restaurant.

288
00:10:05,777 --> 00:10:06,777
(The first one is a sundae restaurant?)

289
00:10:06,777 --> 00:10:08,817
I didn't think this could be it.

290
00:10:09,217 --> 00:10:10,487
(A fusion sundae dish related to India?)

291
00:10:10,487 --> 00:10:12,147
(Aren't you supposed to mix them?)

292
00:10:12,147 --> 00:10:14,617
(It's like Indian meets Korean, right?)

293
00:10:14,617 --> 00:10:16,817
- It's kind of...
- What?

294
00:10:17,687 --> 00:10:19,087
It doesn't look like it from the outside.

295
00:10:19,087 --> 00:10:20,927
The exterior gives no hint of that.

296
00:10:20,927 --> 00:10:22,227
It's just your typical sundae place.

297
00:10:22,227 --> 00:10:23,927
(They head inside, full of suspicion.)

298
00:10:23,927 --> 00:10:25,097
It's...

299
00:10:25,727 --> 00:10:27,637
(Tucked away in an alley in the heart of Gangnam)

300
00:10:27,637 --> 00:10:29,737
The outside of the restaurant isn't all that...

301
00:10:29,737 --> 00:10:30,867
unique or anything.

302
00:10:30,937 --> 00:10:32,307
It looks normal.

303
00:10:32,307 --> 00:10:33,837
(An ordinary-looking restaurant)

304
00:10:33,837 --> 00:10:35,937
This place feels like an old place...

305
00:10:35,937 --> 00:10:38,047
- with numerous experiences.
- Exactly.

306
00:10:38,047 --> 00:10:40,477
- I had my doubts, you know?
- Same here.

307
00:10:40,477 --> 00:10:41,577
(A space that speaks of years of experience)

308
00:10:41,747 --> 00:10:43,477
See that menu item hidden behind a question mark?

309
00:10:43,477 --> 00:10:45,847
- It must be a special dish.
- Maybe it's a sort of sundae stew.

310
00:10:46,487 --> 00:10:48,917
(What's the surprisingly perfect fusion...)

311
00:10:48,917 --> 00:10:50,557
(of sundae and Indian cuisine?)

312
00:10:51,057 --> 00:10:52,857
Does that mean...

313
00:10:52,857 --> 00:10:54,857
- we're having gukbap?
- What's wrong?

314
00:10:54,857 --> 00:10:55,957
I love it.

315
00:10:56,257 --> 00:10:57,927
(Moved)

316
00:10:57,927 --> 00:11:01,267
Seriously, BIBI has been coming on this show just to eat.

317
00:11:01,867 --> 00:11:04,407
(As expected of Foodie BIBI)

318
00:11:04,407 --> 00:11:06,667
- Let's sit, Sung Tae.
- She's in full-on eating mode.

319
00:11:06,667 --> 00:11:08,937
(They quickly sit down, ready to watch BIBI dig in!)

320
00:11:09,137 --> 00:11:11,847
But the inside of this place...

321
00:11:12,807 --> 00:11:14,377
isn't giving any Indian vibes.

322
00:11:14,377 --> 00:11:17,947
(Clue to note: No trace of India in the decor)

323
00:11:18,087 --> 00:11:20,347
You could easily make this a fake restaurant.

324
00:11:20,857 --> 00:11:22,417
- Exactly.
- It'd be easy peasy.

325
00:11:22,417 --> 00:11:23,927
- It's perfect to be a fake spot.
- Right?

326
00:11:23,927 --> 00:11:25,487
(All it takes is adding a fake menu item.)

327
00:11:25,487 --> 00:11:26,587
It looks fake.

328
00:11:27,557 --> 00:11:29,657
- How about we call over the owner?
- Sure.

329
00:11:29,657 --> 00:11:30,727
Excuse me!

330
00:11:31,227 --> 00:11:33,167
(Curious)

331
00:11:33,167 --> 00:11:34,637
- Hello, sir.
- Hi.

332
00:11:34,637 --> 00:11:35,997
- Hi.
- Hi, sir.

333
00:11:36,197 --> 00:11:38,067
- Hi, nice to meet you.
- Hi.

334
00:11:38,067 --> 00:11:39,137
This restaurant seems...

335
00:11:39,137 --> 00:11:41,977
just like your typical sundae soup place.

336
00:11:41,977 --> 00:11:42,977
Right.

337
00:11:42,977 --> 00:11:44,577
Is there something special about it?

338
00:11:44,577 --> 00:11:45,607
We heard...

339
00:11:45,607 --> 00:11:47,007
- there was something Indian.
- Exactly.

340
00:11:47,247 --> 00:11:51,187
We serve curry sundae stew...

341
00:11:51,187 --> 00:11:52,347
and kkakdugi sundae stew.

342
00:11:52,347 --> 00:11:53,347
(Surprised)

343
00:11:53,957 --> 00:11:55,987
- Curry sundae stew?
- Kkakdugi stew?

344
00:11:55,987 --> 00:11:58,587
(What are they?)

345
00:11:58,687 --> 00:12:01,397
My parents opened this restaurant...

346
00:12:01,397 --> 00:12:04,597
in 1995 and spent 30 years...

347
00:12:04,597 --> 00:12:07,637
serving sundae stew in the same location.

348
00:12:08,067 --> 00:12:11,667
I left my job in 2024 and took over the restaurant.

349
00:12:12,207 --> 00:12:14,407
Customers often ask why we call it...

350
00:12:14,407 --> 00:12:16,737
sundae stew, not sundae soup.

351
00:12:17,207 --> 00:12:19,407
Back then, sundae soup was seen...

352
00:12:19,407 --> 00:12:22,517
as an affordable, familiar soup...

353
00:12:22,517 --> 00:12:25,217
you'd enjoy in a market alley.

354
00:12:25,217 --> 00:12:27,857
My parents wanted to create a premium version...

355
00:12:27,857 --> 00:12:29,417
(Fresh meat)

356
00:12:29,417 --> 00:12:31,127
with high-quality meat...

357
00:12:31,187 --> 00:12:32,987
and a rich, hearty broth.

358
00:12:32,987 --> 00:12:35,297
That's why they named it sundae stew.

359
00:12:35,297 --> 00:12:36,827
(A rich sundae stew perfected over 30 years)

360
00:12:36,827 --> 00:12:39,897
Our curry and kkakdugi sundae stews are...

361
00:12:39,897 --> 00:12:43,567
special dishes that pair beautifully with our signature rich broth.

362
00:12:44,067 --> 00:12:46,067
Have you ever tried sundae stew like this?

363
00:12:46,067 --> 00:12:48,307
From curry sundae stew to kkakdugi sundae stew.

364
00:12:48,307 --> 00:12:50,477
Sundae soup gets a seriously impressive makeover!

365
00:12:50,477 --> 00:12:53,047
Sixth Sense crew, is this menu real?

366
00:12:53,047 --> 00:12:55,377
(Sixth Sense crew, is this menu real?)

367
00:12:56,817 --> 00:12:59,487
How did you come up with curry sundae stew?

368
00:12:59,487 --> 00:13:01,217
My parents came up with the dish...

369
00:13:01,217 --> 00:13:05,457
simply because turmeric and curry...

370
00:13:05,457 --> 00:13:07,187
are good for your health.

371
00:13:07,187 --> 00:13:09,957
Customers had a fixed idea of what sundae soup should be,

372
00:13:09,957 --> 00:13:12,267
- Right.
- so the dish wasn't very popular.

373
00:13:12,267 --> 00:13:14,937
But during COVID-19, word spread that curry was good...

374
00:13:14,937 --> 00:13:16,767
- for your immune system.
- Yes.

375
00:13:16,767 --> 00:13:18,367
- I remember.
- Turmeric.

376
00:13:18,367 --> 00:13:21,577
Now, over half of our customers...

377
00:13:21,577 --> 00:13:22,707
order that dish.

378
00:13:23,277 --> 00:13:24,547
- Really?
- Yes.

379
00:13:24,747 --> 00:13:26,807
- Seriously?
- Really?

380
00:13:28,147 --> 00:13:30,147
But why haven't I heard of it before?

381
00:13:32,087 --> 00:13:33,447
What's the difference between turmeric and wild turmeric?

382
00:13:33,447 --> 00:13:34,457
(Surprise question)

383
00:13:34,457 --> 00:13:35,517
(Surprised)

384
00:13:35,517 --> 00:13:37,657
A quiz? A test?

385
00:13:37,657 --> 00:13:38,657
(Sung Tae's surprise question?)

386
00:13:38,957 --> 00:13:40,627
- A quiz? A test?
- It's nothing.

387
00:13:42,527 --> 00:13:43,527
(Laughing)

388
00:13:43,527 --> 00:13:45,197
Ask with confidence.

389
00:13:45,197 --> 00:13:47,637
I just asked because it felt too fake.

390
00:13:47,637 --> 00:13:48,697
Was that why?

391
00:13:48,997 --> 00:13:50,837
So what's the difference between the two?

392
00:13:51,437 --> 00:13:53,067
Foreigners call it wild turmeric,

393
00:13:53,067 --> 00:13:55,737
while Koreans... No, foreigners call it turmeric,

394
00:13:55,737 --> 00:13:58,377
while Koreans call it wild turmeric.

395
00:13:58,377 --> 00:13:59,447
That was what I heard.

396
00:13:59,447 --> 00:14:01,177
- Like kiwi and kiwiberry, right?
- But they're the same.

397
00:14:01,177 --> 00:14:02,277
The two are the same.

398
00:14:02,917 --> 00:14:03,917
That's interesting.

399
00:14:04,047 --> 00:14:06,717
We'll double-check before airing that part, okay?

400
00:14:07,117 --> 00:14:08,817
Yes, absolutely.

401
00:14:08,817 --> 00:14:10,087
After double-checking.

402
00:14:10,087 --> 00:14:12,327
That just now was Heo Sung Tae's personal answer.

403
00:14:12,327 --> 00:14:14,097
- It's not an official statement.
- What Sung Tae said has...

404
00:14:14,097 --> 00:14:16,027
- nothing to do with us.
- It's not.

405
00:14:16,027 --> 00:14:17,567
- It's only his opinion.
- Double-check it.

406
00:14:17,567 --> 00:14:18,567
I wanted to see...

407
00:14:18,567 --> 00:14:19,567
- the owner's reaction.
- It was a guess, right?

408
00:14:19,567 --> 00:14:20,767
- His expression?
- Yes.

409
00:14:20,767 --> 00:14:22,637
- When asked the question?
- That was funny.

410
00:14:22,767 --> 00:14:24,067
Are you usually perceptive?

411
00:14:24,067 --> 00:14:25,067
No.

412
00:14:26,467 --> 00:14:28,177
- He's not one bit perceptive.
- No.

413
00:14:28,177 --> 00:14:29,537
I get things wrong all the time.

414
00:14:30,007 --> 00:14:31,247
Sung Tae isn't perceptive at all.

415
00:14:31,247 --> 00:14:34,047
- I always lose at Liar Game.
- Is that so?

416
00:14:34,417 --> 00:14:35,977
Wasn't there another dish?

417
00:14:35,977 --> 00:14:37,047
You mentioned...

418
00:14:37,047 --> 00:14:38,087
- Yes, kkakdugi sundae stew.
- kkakdugi sundae stew.

419
00:14:38,087 --> 00:14:39,247
- Yes.
- What's that?

420
00:14:39,247 --> 00:14:40,617
When it comes to kkakdugi sundae stew...

421
00:14:40,617 --> 00:14:41,987
Some customers...

422
00:14:41,987 --> 00:14:43,957
- pour kkakdugi juice...
- Yes, the juice.

423
00:14:43,957 --> 00:14:45,687
into their sundae soup.

424
00:14:45,687 --> 00:14:47,457
It's a hassle to add it every time,

425
00:14:47,457 --> 00:14:48,857
- So the juice is already in it.
- so they asked...

426
00:14:48,857 --> 00:14:50,227
if we could cook it with the soup.

427
00:14:50,227 --> 00:14:51,327
(It sounds good!)

428
00:14:51,327 --> 00:14:52,927
- Oh, my!
- It sounds good.

429
00:14:52,927 --> 00:14:53,967
(Surprised)

430
00:14:53,967 --> 00:14:55,537
(Impressed)

431
00:14:55,797 --> 00:14:57,067
(His mouth is watering.)

432
00:14:57,067 --> 00:15:00,237
Kkakdugi sundae stew has its own loyal fanbase.

433
00:15:00,237 --> 00:15:01,237
I bet.

434
00:15:01,237 --> 00:15:03,777
Those who like it always order it.

435
00:15:04,407 --> 00:15:05,877
- It sounds good.
- Right?

436
00:15:05,877 --> 00:15:08,647
- You can't go wrong with it.
- For breakfast, gukbap is...

437
00:15:08,647 --> 00:15:09,717
It's the best.

438
00:15:10,017 --> 00:15:12,187
- Could we try some?
- Of course.

439
00:15:12,187 --> 00:15:13,517
- Nice. We'll leave it to you.
- We'll leave it to you.

440
00:15:13,517 --> 00:15:14,857
- Thank you.
- I'll be right back.

441
00:15:14,857 --> 00:15:15,857
(How will the premium sundae stew taste?)

442
00:15:15,857 --> 00:15:17,487
My mouth didn't water at curry sundae stew,

443
00:15:17,487 --> 00:15:18,957
- but for kkakdugi sundae stew...
- The kkakdugi, right?

444
00:15:19,287 --> 00:15:21,097
My mouth is watering, telling me it's real.

445
00:15:21,097 --> 00:15:22,227
- Me too.
- I'm serious.

446
00:15:22,227 --> 00:15:23,697
- We're Koreans through and through.
- It's a familiar taste.

447
00:15:23,697 --> 00:15:26,327
Do you start the show on a positive note?

448
00:15:26,327 --> 00:15:28,137
- Aren't you suspicious of anything?
- We need to be.

449
00:15:28,137 --> 00:15:29,567
I find so many things suspicious.

450
00:15:29,567 --> 00:15:30,767
- Like what?
- Like what?

451
00:15:30,767 --> 00:15:33,637
Jokbal seems out of place at a sundae soup restaurant.

452
00:15:33,637 --> 00:15:34,907
You're right.

453
00:15:34,907 --> 00:15:36,207
(Jokbal at a restaurant specialising in sundae doesn't go well.)

454
00:15:36,207 --> 00:15:39,007
What's more, the regular sundae stew is 13 dollars.

455
00:15:39,007 --> 00:15:41,577
The other dishes must have extra ingredients,

456
00:15:41,577 --> 00:15:43,317
but they're all 13 dollars too.

457
00:15:43,317 --> 00:15:46,347
There could be B-Sides hidden among them,

458
00:15:46,347 --> 00:15:47,347
- so we must look carefully.
- You're right.

459
00:15:47,657 --> 00:15:49,157
Consider today's theme.

460
00:15:49,157 --> 00:15:51,027
It's "We actually make a pretty good pair."

461
00:15:51,027 --> 00:15:52,727
(Looking attentively)

462
00:15:53,157 --> 00:15:55,357
Do we say it now, not later?

463
00:15:55,357 --> 00:15:56,697
- About what?
- When something feels wrong.

464
00:15:56,697 --> 00:15:57,967
- Whenever you notice something.
- Right away.

465
00:15:57,967 --> 00:15:59,097
If you mention it later,

466
00:15:59,097 --> 00:16:00,867
you might end up going home without saying anything.

467
00:16:00,867 --> 00:16:02,137
The way the milk and Coke are arranged is weird.

468
00:16:02,137 --> 00:16:03,667
- Totally, I saw it earlier.
- It's too weird.

469
00:16:03,667 --> 00:16:04,667
Right?

470
00:16:04,667 --> 00:16:06,737
(Milk and Coke...)

471
00:16:06,737 --> 00:16:11,547
(in a sundae stew restaurant's fridge?)

472
00:16:11,747 --> 00:16:12,847
That sure is weird.

473
00:16:13,247 --> 00:16:15,177
I think that's just absurd.

474
00:16:15,647 --> 00:16:16,717
Why are they arranged like that?

475
00:16:16,717 --> 00:16:18,017
If you take...

476
00:16:18,017 --> 00:16:21,257
the first letters of milk and Coke, you get MC.

477
00:16:22,187 --> 00:16:23,187
(Laughing)

478
00:16:23,187 --> 00:16:25,927
(Embarrassed)

479
00:16:26,057 --> 00:16:27,857
What? What is it?

480
00:16:27,857 --> 00:16:28,897
(Stay confident, BIBI!)

481
00:16:28,897 --> 00:16:29,897
That's a B-Side.

482
00:16:29,897 --> 00:16:32,167
- A B-Side, no doubt.
- It's a B-Side.

483
00:16:32,167 --> 00:16:33,667
It's definitely a B-Side,

484
00:16:33,667 --> 00:16:35,137
but it's hard to figure out what it means yet.

485
00:16:35,137 --> 00:16:37,267
- Yes.
- But the clues add up...

486
00:16:37,267 --> 00:16:38,737
and connect to form one B-Side.

487
00:16:38,737 --> 00:16:39,867
(Are the milk and Coke today's B-Side?)

488
00:16:40,337 --> 00:16:43,137
Don't you normally say sundae soup, not stew?

489
00:16:43,237 --> 00:16:44,977
It's called stew when you simmer...

490
00:16:44,977 --> 00:16:46,247
the bones to make the broth.

491
00:16:46,577 --> 00:16:47,947
You simmer beef bones for beef bone soup, right?

492
00:16:47,947 --> 00:16:49,047
- Is that the difference?
- Yes, like seolleongtang...

493
00:16:49,047 --> 00:16:50,177
and beef bone soup.

494
00:16:50,177 --> 00:16:51,947
Sundae stew must use bone broth.

495
00:16:51,947 --> 00:16:53,147
Is that so?

496
00:16:54,117 --> 00:16:56,817
What's the difference between sundae stew and sundae soup?

497
00:16:56,817 --> 00:16:57,987
He's double-checking.

498
00:16:59,327 --> 00:17:01,757
Really, what's up with you?

499
00:17:02,257 --> 00:17:04,167
It's just something I randomly said.

500
00:17:04,167 --> 00:17:07,027
If Sang Jin ends up being wrong even after double-checking...

501
00:17:07,027 --> 00:17:09,697
"Sundae soup and sundae stew..."

502
00:17:09,697 --> 00:17:11,337
- Different names?
- "have..."

503
00:17:11,467 --> 00:17:13,607
"different names, but they're the same dish."

504
00:17:14,807 --> 00:17:16,707
See? It's only a difference in name.

505
00:17:16,707 --> 00:17:17,977
Sung Tae was right about it.

506
00:17:17,977 --> 00:17:19,977
What did Sang Jin say earlier?

507
00:17:19,977 --> 00:17:21,447
That it's called stew because the bones are simmered.

508
00:17:21,677 --> 00:17:22,847
Why are you being mean, Jae Seok?

509
00:17:22,847 --> 00:17:24,617
I was about to go around repeating that.

510
00:17:24,617 --> 00:17:25,647
(She almost acts like she knows about it well somewhere else.)

511
00:17:25,647 --> 00:17:26,817
Even my ears have turned red.

