- We have to figure them out.

764
00:25:58,427 --> 00:25:59,467
We can't figure it out...

765
00:25:59,467 --> 00:26:01,097
- from this alone.
- We've become much smarter.

766
00:26:01,097 --> 00:26:03,337
I know, right? We get smarter with every episode.

767
00:26:03,337 --> 00:26:04,907
We're smart only when we get it right.

768
00:26:05,337 --> 00:26:06,337
(Glaring)

769
00:26:06,337 --> 00:26:07,837
Stop spoiling the mood.

770
00:26:08,307 --> 00:26:09,907
Think of how far we've come.

771
00:26:09,907 --> 00:26:11,847
Don't forget where we started.

772
00:26:11,847 --> 00:26:12,907
Really.

773
00:26:12,907 --> 00:26:14,107
- What could it be?
- Bruce Lee.

774
00:26:14,107 --> 00:26:15,447
- Milk.
- Why is Bruce Lee here?

775
00:26:15,447 --> 00:26:16,577
- Bruce Lee.
- Seoul Bruce.

776
00:26:17,447 --> 00:26:20,617
My gut is telling me that place is real.

777
00:26:20,847 --> 00:26:22,057
But then, curry sundae stew?

778
00:26:22,387 --> 00:26:24,517
It's a dish you could easily add.

779
00:26:24,927 --> 00:26:25,927
Bruce Lee?

780
00:26:26,787 --> 00:26:28,197
- Bruce Lee...
- Why is Bruce Lee...

781
00:26:28,197 --> 00:26:29,397
Bruce Lee wore yellow.

782
00:26:29,997 --> 00:26:31,057
- He wore a yellow tracksuit.
- Tracksuit?

783
00:26:31,057 --> 00:26:32,067
- Tracksuit?
- You could be right.

784
00:26:32,067 --> 00:26:33,167
For real.

785
00:26:34,297 --> 00:26:36,767
Now that I think about it, Bruce Lee's yellow tracksuit...

786
00:26:36,767 --> 00:26:38,607
could point to the yellow curry.

787
00:26:39,137 --> 00:26:41,237
(Is Bruce Lee's yellow outfit...)

788
00:26:41,237 --> 00:26:43,977
(a B-Side suggesting the curry sundae stew is fake?)

789
00:26:44,307 --> 00:26:48,817
The production crew no longer gives us easy clues.

790
00:26:49,447 --> 00:26:51,647
We should check out the 2nd and 3rd places 1st.

791
00:26:51,647 --> 00:26:53,947
- They have to connect, right?
- Yes.

792
00:26:54,217 --> 00:26:56,817
Sang Jin, you're sitting like you're on your sofa at home.

793
00:26:56,817 --> 00:26:58,857
I'm worried the camera won't be able to see Eun I.

794
00:26:58,857 --> 00:27:00,187
- She has her own camera.
- I have a camera.

795
00:27:00,187 --> 00:27:01,357
- Is that so?
- Yes. Don't worry, Sang Jin.

796
00:27:01,357 --> 00:27:02,397
- I'm sorry.
- No problem.

797
00:27:02,627 --> 00:27:04,297
Sang Jin is old-school now.

798
00:27:04,727 --> 00:27:05,767
Back in the day,

799
00:27:05,767 --> 00:27:06,997
the cameraman would scold you for blocking someone.

800
00:27:06,997 --> 00:27:08,537
Exactly, I was worried I'd get scolded.

801
00:27:08,537 --> 00:27:09,597
Right? "Why did you..."

802
00:27:09,597 --> 00:27:11,267
"block Eun I from the camera?"

803
00:27:11,267 --> 00:27:13,107
- Things have changed.
- I see.

804
00:27:13,107 --> 00:27:15,577
- I'm sorry.
- We aim to keep things natural.

805
00:27:16,707 --> 00:27:18,507
- Are you saying I'm unnatural?
- Yes.

806
00:27:18,507 --> 00:27:20,007
My goodness.

807
00:27:20,377 --> 00:27:22,747
I was helping Eun I get on camera, okay?

808
00:27:23,677 --> 00:27:25,887
This place has to do with talismans, right?

809
00:27:27,187 --> 00:27:30,057
(A spot-on fortune-telling shrine...)

810
00:27:30,057 --> 00:27:32,887
(with talismans that are works of art!)

811
00:27:33,827 --> 00:27:35,257
"The shaman even does this!"

812
00:27:35,527 --> 00:27:37,697
Right. There was something about a shaman.

813
00:27:38,397 --> 00:27:39,627
Shall we get off now?

814
00:27:39,627 --> 00:27:41,497
(What could possibly pair well with a shamanic reading?)

815
00:27:41,897 --> 00:27:44,267
The outside looks like an ordinary house.

816
00:27:44,667 --> 00:27:46,607
- It's a house.
- Isn't it a residential area?

817
00:27:46,707 --> 00:27:47,937
It's a house.

818
00:27:48,307 --> 00:27:50,577
(A densely packed residential neighbourhood)

819
00:27:50,577 --> 00:27:51,907
This itself is a little too...

820
00:27:53,307 --> 00:27:54,307
Hold on.

821
00:27:54,307 --> 00:27:55,577
(They enter quietly, mindful of the other residents.)

822
00:27:55,577 --> 00:27:57,277
Quiet. Lower your voice.

823
00:27:57,277 --> 00:27:59,447
(What awaits inside this unit in a multifamily building?)

824
00:27:59,447 --> 00:28:00,447
Seriously.

825
00:28:00,947 --> 00:28:02,887
- What could it be?
- A shrine?

826
00:28:03,117 --> 00:28:05,087
It's a shrine.

827
00:28:05,827 --> 00:28:07,287
(Through the front door)

828
00:28:07,287 --> 00:28:09,557
(Past an ordinary-looking entryway)

829
00:28:10,057 --> 00:28:13,467
(A shrine fills the entire living room.)

830
00:28:13,967 --> 00:28:15,737
- What could this be?
- What...

831
00:28:15,737 --> 00:28:16,867
(At first glance, it looks like a typical shamanic shrine.)

832
00:28:16,867 --> 00:28:18,537
As mentioned earlier,

833
00:28:18,537 --> 00:28:20,837
the shaman writes talismans for you here, right?

834
00:28:21,167 --> 00:28:22,577
I saw those brushes.

835
00:28:22,577 --> 00:28:24,537
- Me too. Something was written...
- It's how I picture a shrine.

836
00:28:25,047 --> 00:28:26,547
- Gosh.
- This is scary.

837
00:28:26,547 --> 00:28:28,677
Do shrines normally have toy cars and such?

838
00:28:29,347 --> 00:28:31,217
Don't those look out of place?

839
00:28:31,217 --> 00:28:32,247
Yes, they do.

840
00:28:32,247 --> 00:28:34,447
Chupa Chups and those cars.

841
00:28:34,447 --> 00:28:37,187
(Toy cars and sweet lollipops?)

842
00:28:37,187 --> 00:28:39,587
- Aren't they for the Child Spirit?
- Really?

843
00:28:39,587 --> 00:28:40,987
- Even the cars?
- Yes.

844
00:28:40,987 --> 00:28:42,497
(Toys, snacks, and even alcohol. What are they all for?)

845
00:28:42,497 --> 00:28:44,657
Visually speaking, it's a bit...

846
00:28:44,657 --> 00:28:46,367
(Toys, snacks, and even alcohol. What are they all for?)

847
00:28:46,427 --> 00:28:48,437
The strong smell in here...

848
00:28:48,437 --> 00:28:50,367
can't possibly be fake.

849
00:28:51,297 --> 00:28:53,607
- Shall we call the owner over?
- Can the talismans be fake?

850
00:28:53,607 --> 00:28:54,877
- It's a bit...
- Let's call them over.

851
00:28:55,207 --> 00:28:56,637
Excuse me, please come out.

852
00:28:57,777 --> 00:28:58,877
- Oh, my.
- Is she here?

853
00:28:58,877 --> 00:29:00,077
- Ma'am.
- Hi.

854
00:29:00,077 --> 00:29:01,247
- Hi.
- Hi.

855
00:29:02,117 --> 00:29:03,347
She wasn't here earlier.

856
00:29:04,317 --> 00:29:07,387
Playing a shaman would actually be easy.

857
00:29:07,387 --> 00:29:09,257
- For an actor or actress.
- Really?

858
00:29:09,957 --> 00:29:11,387
(Unfazed by their suspicions,)

859
00:29:11,387 --> 00:29:13,227
(the shaman continues praying.)

860
00:29:13,557 --> 00:29:14,727
I've never been anywhere like this before.

861
00:29:14,727 --> 00:29:16,597
- Hi.
- Hi.

862
00:29:17,097 --> 00:29:19,067
- Nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you.

863
00:29:19,567 --> 00:29:22,197
We heard this place was famous...

864
00:29:22,197 --> 00:29:24,797
and that the talismans...

865
00:29:24,797 --> 00:29:26,037
- were unique.
- Correct.

866
00:29:26,037 --> 00:29:28,277
Let me introduce myself first.

867
00:29:28,607 --> 00:29:30,377
I write coloured talismans.

868
00:29:30,377 --> 00:29:33,107
I read the energy of different colours...

869
00:29:33,177 --> 00:29:35,947
and help people restore balance where their energy...

870
00:29:35,947 --> 00:29:37,377
- is lacking.
- Colour?

871
00:29:37,377 --> 00:29:39,647
- So you write talismans with colour?
- Yes.

872
00:29:39,787 --> 00:29:43,157
Hi. I'm Keum Heon, a shaman who reads fortunes...

873
00:29:43,257 --> 00:29:45,487
through the energy of colours and creates...

874
00:29:45,487 --> 00:29:46,987
personalised coloured talismans.

875
00:29:47,287 --> 00:29:50,657
I serve several deities at my shrine.

876
00:29:50,897 --> 00:29:54,197
The one who gives me the most spiritual messages is...

877
00:29:54,197 --> 00:29:55,837
the Scholar Spirit.

878
00:29:55,837 --> 00:29:57,267
(It's the Scholar Spirit.)

879
00:29:57,267 --> 00:30:01,107
Shamans who serve the Scholar Spirit tend to have...

880
00:30:01,307 --> 00:30:04,237
strong ties to writing and written characters.

881
00:30:04,407 --> 00:30:07,707
In my case, I take a closer look at the energy of colours...

882
00:30:08,277 --> 00:30:10,817
and read people's fortunes...

883
00:30:10,817 --> 00:30:13,647
while personally writing talismans suited to each individual's energy.

884
00:30:13,647 --> 00:30:15,457
(Colour talismans customized for each client)

885
00:30:15,687 --> 00:30:17,817
Have you ever seen colour talismans?

886
00:30:17,817 --> 00:30:19,857
The shaman is incredibly spot on.

887
00:30:19,957 --> 00:30:22,657
Hurry up and visit her before she becomes even more famous!

888
00:30:23,027 --> 00:30:26,067
Sixth Sense crew, is this place real?

889
00:30:26,067 --> 00:30:28,297
(Sixth Sense crew, is this place real?)

890
00:30:28,867 --> 00:30:32,337
How do you read the fortune from the colours?

891
00:30:32,707 --> 00:30:34,907
Each and everyone has...

892
00:30:34,907 --> 00:30:37,577
- their own unique colour.
- Really?

893
00:30:37,577 --> 00:30:40,147
I feel its energy...

894
00:30:40,147 --> 00:30:42,377
and listen to the deity.

895
00:30:42,517 --> 00:30:44,717
That's how I complement each aspect.

896
00:30:44,717 --> 00:30:47,117
So you read the fortune based on the colours?

897
00:30:47,117 --> 00:30:50,187
That's right. For example, rather than Four Pillars of Destiny,

898
00:30:50,387 --> 00:30:52,057
I trust the scenery I see.

899
00:30:52,057 --> 00:30:53,527
Do you look through a tool or something?

900
00:30:53,527 --> 00:30:54,957
- No, just my bare eyes.
- You call it scenery?

901
00:30:54,957 --> 00:30:56,797
- Yes, I call it scenery.
- That's the term you use.

902
00:30:56,897 --> 00:31:01,227
From there, I observe what your unique colour is.

903
00:31:01,367 --> 00:31:04,037
To help you understand,

904
00:31:04,037 --> 00:31:05,337
blue signifies...

905
00:31:05,337 --> 00:31:08,677
a new start or a challenge.

906
00:31:08,737 --> 00:31:11,277
As for red,

907
00:31:11,277 --> 00:31:14,307
it signifies passion and fame.

908
00:31:14,377 --> 00:31:16,317
Yellow signifies...

909
00:31:16,317 --> 00:31:18,447
wealth and honour.

910
00:31:18,447 --> 00:31:21,917
White signifies a lover, a fated person,

911
00:31:22,417 --> 00:31:24,557
or a new contract.

912
00:31:24,557 --> 00:31:27,827
Black signifies rest...

913
00:31:28,057 --> 00:31:30,357
or a period of stability.

914
00:31:32,167 --> 00:31:34,027
Kyoung Pyo looks like he has a lot to say.

915
00:31:34,327 --> 00:31:35,867
He's caught something with his hawk eye.

916
00:31:35,867 --> 00:31:36,867
(Did Kyoung Pyo spot something?)

917
00:31:37,137 --> 00:31:39,037
Forgive me if I sound rude,

918
00:31:39,067 --> 00:31:43,577
but could you be a personal colour analyst?

919
00:31:43,577 --> 00:31:45,077
That's possible.

920
00:31:45,077 --> 00:31:47,447
- Cool or warm undertones?
- Yes.

921
00:31:47,447 --> 00:31:49,317
Those who analyse the colours that suit you?

922
00:31:49,817 --> 00:31:51,617
You're sharp.

923
00:31:51,987 --> 00:31:54,487
Since when did you start this job?

924
00:31:54,787 --> 00:31:57,857
I've started only recently. I'm still new.

925
00:31:57,857 --> 00:32:00,227
If I may explain a bit about myself...

926
00:32:00,427 --> 00:32:02,557
- I was actually an athlete.
- What?

927
00:32:02,557 --> 00:32:05,297
I majored in sports at the university,

928
00:32:05,297 --> 00:32:08,167
and I worked as an instructor at a sports center.

929
00:32:08,797 --> 00:32:12,367
But since 5 years ago, in 2021,

930
00:32:12,567 --> 00:32:16,837
I started feeling the energy around the students.

931
00:32:16,837 --> 00:32:19,777
- Red and...
- It's chakra.

932
00:32:19,777 --> 00:32:21,247
Red energy.

933
00:32:21,247 --> 00:32:23,947
- I saw red aura around them.
- Really?

934
00:32:24,417 --> 00:32:27,747
Or I saw black fog-like thing under them.

935
00:32:27,987 --> 00:32:30,217
I started to have visual-hallucination-like visions.

936
00:32:30,787 --> 00:32:34,357
And just at that time, I started feeling really sick.

937
00:32:34,627 --> 00:32:36,397
I've gone from one university hospital to another...

938
00:32:36,397 --> 00:32:38,127
for two years.

939
00:32:38,467 --> 00:32:40,767
They'd say I have a certain disease,

940
00:32:40,767 --> 00:32:43,397
but when I got treated, it turned out it wasn't the problem.

941
00:32:43,967 --> 00:32:48,037
So I thought, "Perhaps I should go and get my fortune told."

942
00:32:48,037 --> 00:32:50,477
So I went to a shaman, and I was told...

943
00:32:50,707 --> 00:32:52,647
that I needed to receive a spirit.

944
00:32:53,177 --> 00:32:56,547
Back then, it felt like my whole world came crashing down.

945
00:32:56,547 --> 00:32:58,077
It was so hard.

946
00:33:02,657 --> 00:33:04,587
My parents were very against it too.

947
00:33:05,157 --> 00:33:07,287
I even did a ritual to prevent receiving a spirit,

948
00:33:07,287 --> 00:33:10,497
but it didn't work, so in the end...

949
00:33:10,497 --> 00:33:12,227
- I'm sorry.
- Don't be.

950
00:33:12,597 --> 00:33:15,897
You must've remembered the times of...

951
00:33:16,097 --> 00:33:19,037
your personal struggles and considerations...

952
00:33:19,037 --> 00:33:20,437
that you got choked up.

953
00:33:20,667 --> 00:33:23,177
On the other hand, due to the nature of the show,

954
00:33:23,177 --> 00:33:25,247
we can't help but think if this is part of the act too.

955
00:33:25,447 --> 00:33:26,907
Please understand.

956
00:33:26,907 --> 00:33:28,917
I only thought about it in my mind.

957
00:33:28,917 --> 00:33:31,377
- Just in case.
- They could be real tears, but...

958
00:33:32,017 --> 00:33:33,087
- I'm okay.
- Did you watch...

959
00:33:33,087 --> 00:33:34,117
Han Sang Jin's One-Point?

960
00:33:34,117 --> 00:33:35,657
- Pardon?
- Sorry, it's nothing.

961
00:33:35,657 --> 00:33:36,687
She isn't an actress.

962
00:33:36,687 --> 00:33:37,957
- What didn't she watch?
- If she were an actress...

963
00:33:37,957 --> 00:33:39,387
I have a YouTube channel called Han Sang Jin's One-Point...

964
00:33:39,387 --> 00:33:40,857
where I give acting lessons.

965
00:33:40,857 --> 00:33:42,057
Most actors watch that.

966
00:33:42,757 --> 00:33:44,897
- Most do.
- Sang Jin.

967
00:33:44,897 --> 00:33:46,967
- Deluded Jin!
- Bit part actors watch it!

968
00:33:46,967 --> 00:33:48,997
- Twenty thousand people watch it.
- Stop with your delusions.

969
00:33:48,997 --> 00:33:50,437
You watched Han Sang Jin's One-Point, right?

970
00:33:50,667 --> 00:33:52,807
- Everyone watches it.
- Stop with your delusions.

971
00:33:53,007 --> 00:33:54,567
Now you know why he's called Deluded Jin.

972
00:33:54,737 --> 00:33:57,207
I'm sorry. If I was rude, please excuse me.

973
00:33:57,377 --> 00:33:59,147
- This is...
- Yes.

974
00:33:59,377 --> 00:34:02,177
You talked about colours. Do you see colours around us too?

975
00:34:02,247 --> 00:34:03,317
Yes, I'm seeing them now.

976
00:34:03,317 --> 00:34:04,377
- Is that so?
- Yes.

977
00:34:04,647 --> 00:34:06,587
Actually, when I was explaining,

978
00:34:06,587 --> 00:34:08,787
I looked to this side many times.

979
00:34:09,017 --> 00:34:11,787
You're big fire and small fire.

980
00:34:11,787 --> 00:34:13,457
- Big fire and small fire?
- Kyoung Pyo?

981
00:34:13,457 --> 00:34:14,727
Is this "Elemental?"

982
00:34:15,257 --> 00:34:18,157
- "Elemental." - For Kyoung Pyo,

983
00:34:18,297 --> 00:34:19,927
out of all fire, you're the sun.

984
00:34:20,627 --> 00:34:23,597
- That's good, right?
- Yes. You have bright energy.

985
00:34:23,797 --> 00:34:26,407
Even when you're on your own, you have strong energy.

986
00:34:27,037 --> 00:34:28,977
You can stay as is.

987
00:34:29,137 --> 00:34:32,077
But for BIBI... Can I say this?

988
00:34:33,877 --> 00:34:36,077
(What is she going to say?)

989
00:34:36,277 --> 00:34:39,087
How's your chemistry with him on the show?

990
00:34:39,417 --> 00:34:41,447
Nice to meet you.

991
00:34:41,547 --> 00:34:43,717
BIBI is the fire which needs to be handled...

992
00:34:43,917 --> 00:34:45,957
with more sensitivity and care.

993
00:34:46,187 --> 00:34:48,827
So when you stay next to big fire,

994
00:34:48,957 --> 00:34:51,197
you could get hurt often.

995
00:34:51,197 --> 00:34:53,167
- But Kyoung Pyo doesn't know.
- You mean me?

996
00:34:53,167 --> 00:34:54,167
Yes.

997
00:34:54,627 --> 00:34:57,067
- Did it happen?
- Why did you do that?

998
00:34:57,067 --> 00:34:59,367
- I didn't...
- Why did you do that to her?

999
00:34:59,567 --> 00:35:00,737
She's your junior. You can't do that to her.

1000
00:35:00,737 --> 00:35:02,307
If this is fake, I'm going to get hurt.

1001
00:35:02,737 --> 00:35:04,277
I knew from the Four Pillars of Destiny...

1002
00:35:04,277 --> 00:35:05,807
that I was small fire.

1003
00:35:05,807 --> 00:35:08,717
My birthday has small fire.

1004
00:35:08,717 --> 00:35:11,617
You're that...

1005
00:35:14,387 --> 00:35:15,657
- But BIBI.
- You're big fire.

1006
00:35:15,657 --> 00:35:17,317
Why do you keep touching your foot?

1007
00:35:17,317 --> 00:35:19,787
- I'm so... That's not it.
- You must be completely relaxed.

1008
00:35:19,987 --> 00:35:21,257
You better not shake my hand later.

1009
00:35:21,257 --> 00:35:24,127
- They already shook hands.
- You better not shake my hand.

1010
00:35:24,127 --> 00:35:25,897
(Someone has already shaken her hand.)

1011
00:35:25,897 --> 00:35:27,097
She just shook hands with Kyoung Pyo.

1012
00:35:27,097 --> 00:35:28,267
That's not it.

1013
00:35:29,297 --> 00:35:30,867
(Handshake)

1014
00:35:30,867 --> 00:35:32,807
- Kyoung Pyo.
- She shook his hand.

1015
00:35:32,807 --> 00:35:33,867
Since when did you touch your foot?

1016
00:35:33,867 --> 00:35:34,867
I came barefoot...

1017
00:35:34,867 --> 00:35:36,637
because I didn't know we'd be coming to a shrine.

1018
00:35:36,637 --> 00:35:39,277
I kept touching my foot because I wanted to cover it.

1019
00:35:39,477 --> 00:35:41,347
Kyoung Pyo is the one who got hurt.

1020
00:35:41,347 --> 00:35:42,777
Despite him being big fire...

1021
00:35:43,217 --> 00:35:45,917
- Big fire...
- Small fire is hurting big fire.

1022
00:35:46,117 --> 00:35:48,987
Do you have anything you'd like to say about the others?

1023
00:35:49,117 --> 00:35:50,787
I'd like to invite one at a time...

1024
00:35:50,787 --> 00:35:52,787
Then let's start with Sang Jin.

1025
00:35:53,027 --> 00:35:55,357
If this is fake, how did she memorize all this?

1026
00:35:55,357 --> 00:35:56,497
Exactly. How...

1027
00:35:56,997 --> 00:36:00,797
With the colour you're attracted to,

1028
00:36:00,797 --> 00:36:03,197
please write your name and your birthday.

1029
00:36:03,197 --> 00:36:05,667
- I write them?
- Here are pens of five colours.

1030
00:36:05,667 --> 00:36:06,807
(Sang Jin chooses blue.)

1031
00:36:06,967 --> 00:36:09,137
You chose a positive colour.

1032
00:36:10,377 --> 00:36:12,677
Don't most men go for blue?

1033
00:36:12,877 --> 00:36:14,047
I'm 100 percent sure.

1034
00:36:14,577 --> 00:36:16,547
(He writes in blue, dreaming of a new challenge.)

1035
00:36:16,747 --> 00:36:18,177
My handwriting is awesome.

1036
00:36:20,887 --> 00:36:26,227
(She starts telling the fortune by shaking her bells.)

1037
00:36:27,327 --> 00:36:33,297
(What kind of things will she tell him?)

1038
00:36:33,297 --> 00:36:36,437
(To be continued)

1039
00:36:36,437 --> 00:36:37,867
(Stop)

1040
00:36:37,867 --> 00:36:40,937
(Nervous for no reason)

1041
00:36:41,267 --> 00:36:43,707
Do you know why you're drawn to blue?

1042
00:36:43,937 --> 00:36:45,107
- Why?
- Why?

1043
00:36:49,203 --> 00:36:50,603
(Stop)

1044
00:36:50,773 --> 00:36:53,773
(Nervous for no reason)

1045
00:36:54,082 --> 00:36:56,452
Do you know why you're drawn to blue?

1046
00:36:56,722 --> 00:36:57,852
- Why?
- Why?

1047
00:36:58,597 --> 00:37:01,727
I said blue means new starts.

1048
00:37:01,727 --> 00:37:02,767
Yes.

1049
00:37:04,267 --> 00:37:06,367
You have the energy of movement.

1050
00:37:07,207 --> 00:37:08,977
(The energy of shifting?)

1051
00:37:08,977 --> 00:37:12,077
But it's not about moving now. You've already moved.

1052
00:37:12,877 --> 00:37:14,907
You've already moved, right?

1053
00:37:15,047 --> 00:37:16,877
- That's right.
- You've already moved.

1054
00:37:18,177 --> 00:37:21,647
(He's already moved?)

1055
00:37:21,787 --> 00:37:23,417
That's a good site.

1056
00:37:24,887 --> 00:37:26,257
I just recently moved house.

1057
00:37:26,357 --> 00:37:27,487
- Really?
- Yes, for real.

1058
00:37:28,127 --> 00:37:31,427
You'll receive a lot more good energy than your previous home.

1059
00:37:31,597 --> 00:37:33,567
- Really?
- A lot of good things will happen,

1060
00:37:33,567 --> 00:37:34,667
and you'll get the document luck...

1061
00:37:34,667 --> 00:37:36,097
- like contracts.
- You're right.

1062
00:37:36,097 --> 00:37:37,267
I've signed a lot of contracts after moving in.

1063
00:37:37,297 --> 00:37:39,267
You're right. I've signed a lot of contracts after moving in.

1064
00:37:40,237 --> 00:37:42,777
(Goosebumps)

1065
00:37:43,407 --> 00:37:44,407
I'm scared.

1066
00:37:44,407 --> 00:37:45,477
(It is her personal opinion, scientifically unproven.)

1067
00:37:45,647 --> 00:37:47,547
South is better than north,

1068
00:37:47,547 --> 00:37:49,247
and west is better than east.

1069
00:37:49,647 --> 00:37:51,717
So south or southwest.

1070
00:37:51,987 --> 00:37:53,917
Southwest is perfect for you.

1071
00:37:53,917 --> 00:37:55,117
Yes, I moved southwest.

1072
00:37:55,117 --> 00:37:56,857
You said you moved from Haeundae to Dongnae-gu.

1073
00:37:57,017 --> 00:37:59,387
From Haeundae to Dong-gu. That's southwest of Haeundae.

1074
00:37:59,627 --> 00:38:00,827
- That's amazing.
- You're right.

1075
00:38:00,827 --> 00:38:02,157
(She even got the direction of his moving right!)

1076
00:38:02,257 --> 00:38:03,897
It's good for you to stay close to the water.

1077
00:38:03,897 --> 00:38:04,897
- That's right.
- Yes.

1078
00:38:04,957 --> 00:38:06,227
I moved next to Waterfront Park,

1079
00:38:06,227 --> 00:38:07,867
- right next to the sea.
- A park...

1080
00:38:07,867 --> 00:38:09,597
You're telling her everything.

1081
00:38:09,597 --> 00:38:11,797
She probed a bit, and he's telling her everything.

1082
00:38:11,797 --> 00:38:13,737
You might even end up sharing your bank password.

1083
00:38:14,237 --> 00:38:16,207
I mean, it's fascinating. How did you know?

1084
00:38:18,007 --> 00:38:20,547
Normally, the production crew asks the managers in advance.

1085
00:38:20,547 --> 00:38:22,777
- About stuff like this.
- No, I... They ask stuff like that?

1086
00:38:23,117 --> 00:38:24,517
Only my manager knows I've moved.

1087
00:38:24,517 --> 00:38:26,187
- Really?
- And...

1088
00:38:26,787 --> 00:38:28,817
I feel some red energy from you too.

1089
00:38:28,917 --> 00:38:30,457
But what's important is,

1090
00:38:30,687 --> 00:38:33,857
this red energy isn't positive.

1091
00:38:34,357 --> 00:38:35,797
It's related to your health.

1092
00:38:37,657 --> 00:38:39,227
I'll ask the Spirit about this.

1093
00:38:39,227 --> 00:38:41,597
Okay. I suddenly got a herniated disc.

1094
00:38:42,937 --> 00:38:45,867
(She suddenly picks up the brush?)

1095
00:38:46,537 --> 00:38:50,137
(Han)

1096
00:38:50,137 --> 00:38:52,447
- She's good.
- She's so good at writing.

1097
00:38:52,447 --> 00:38:54,747
She has a great calligraphy posture.

1098
00:38:55,777 --> 00:38:58,117
She knows how to do calligraphy.

1099
00:38:59,417 --> 00:39:00,647
Is she a calligrapher?

1100
00:39:02,317 --> 00:39:06,427
(She starts spraying blue ink onto his name.)

1101
00:39:08,587 --> 00:39:12,867
(She shakes the bells again.)

1102
00:39:12,967 --> 00:39:14,827
(Staring intently)

1103
00:39:18,237 --> 00:39:21,437
(What kind of message did she get this time?)

1104
00:39:21,537 --> 00:39:25,607
"It's so suffocating." This is what it said.

1105
00:39:25,877 --> 00:39:27,207
- Really?
- Yes.

1106
00:39:27,207 --> 00:39:29,317
It says it's suffocating.

1107
00:39:30,617 --> 00:39:33,287
You might not feel it,

1108
00:39:33,387 --> 00:39:34,587
but because of it,

1109
00:39:35,587 --> 00:39:37,187
your close one is having a hard time.

1110
00:39:37,417 --> 00:39:38,487
Really?

1111
00:39:39,827 --> 00:39:42,197
- Does he have sleep apnea?
- Maybe.

1112
00:39:42,197 --> 00:39:44,257
Yes, I have sleep apnea. So...

1113
00:39:44,257 --> 00:39:46,067
- Do you have sleep apnea?
- Yes, it's bad.

1114
00:39:46,467 --> 00:39:48,797
I snore very badly, and it gives my wife a very hard time.

1115
00:39:48,797 --> 00:39:49,867
- That should be the case.
- Yes.

1116
00:39:49,867 --> 00:39:51,667
- You must be careful.
- For the 1st time in 22 years...

1117
00:39:51,667 --> 00:39:52,937
of marriage, she suggested we sleep in different rooms...

1118
00:39:53,467 --> 00:39:54,967
because of my snoring.

1119
00:39:55,267 --> 00:39:56,737
You need to be careful.

1120
00:39:56,737 --> 00:39:59,447
You need to take good care of yourself for the time being.

1121
00:39:59,447 --> 00:40:01,677
But you normally take good care of your health.

1122
00:40:01,677 --> 00:40:03,377
Yes. I go for a medical checkup twice a year.

1123
00:40:03,377 --> 00:40:05,517
Right, so for you,

1124
00:40:05,747 --> 00:40:07,947
be more observant, and be more careful...

1125
00:40:07,947 --> 00:40:10,687
so your wife won't be too stressed.

1126
00:40:12,157 --> 00:40:15,387
(The fortune telling is very detailed. Is this place real?)

1127
00:40:15,387 --> 00:40:18,197
- I'll write you a talisman.
- A talisman?

1128
00:40:18,897 --> 00:40:22,437
(She picks up the brush without hesitation.)

1129
00:40:22,897 --> 00:40:26,067
(She writes smoothly as if she's drawing.)

1130
00:40:27,137 --> 00:40:30,337
(Writing in one stroke)

1131
00:40:30,337 --> 00:40:32,807
- Can I ask you a question?
- Yes.

1132
00:40:32,807 --> 00:40:35,577
Did you know Chinese characters well when you did sports too?

1133
00:40:35,577 --> 00:40:37,117
I didn't really know back then.

1134
00:40:37,117 --> 00:40:40,117
I had a terrible handwriting too, since I did sports.

1135
00:40:40,117 --> 00:40:42,857
But as I accepted Scholar Spirit,

1136
00:40:42,857 --> 00:40:45,827
it told me that I had to write too,

1137
00:40:45,827 --> 00:40:47,887
so I started learning it.

1138
00:40:47,887 --> 00:40:49,557
Kyoung Pyo is sharp.

1139
00:40:50,757 --> 00:40:52,797
- He's no joke.
- Again?

1140
00:40:52,797 --> 00:40:53,797
He's very sharp.

1141
00:40:54,267 --> 00:40:55,597
(The talisman is complete.)

1142
00:40:55,597 --> 00:40:56,667
- Thank you.
- It's pretty.

1143
00:40:56,667 --> 00:40:57,697
The talisman...

1144
00:40:57,897 --> 00:41:00,037
The energy escapes every time you open it.

1145
00:41:00,037 --> 00:41:03,537
It's better to keep it enclosed without opening it often.

1146
00:41:03,577 --> 00:41:04,977
- Thank you.
- He'll definitely open it later.

1147
00:41:05,207 --> 00:41:07,547
(Come on.)

1148
00:41:07,877 --> 00:41:09,117
Next, Sung Tae.

1149
00:41:10,277 --> 00:41:11,547
(Grunting)

1150
00:41:11,547 --> 00:41:12,587
(What was that sound?)

1151
00:41:12,587 --> 00:41:14,247
- I heard a strange sound.
- What's wrong?

1152
00:41:14,247 --> 00:41:16,557
- Was that from your back?
- What's wrong?

1153
00:41:16,557 --> 00:41:17,717
My joint.

1154
00:41:17,857 --> 00:41:18,987
Are you trying the way you are told by Jae Seok?

1155
00:41:18,987 --> 00:41:20,527
No, it was my joint.

1156
00:41:21,187 --> 00:41:23,957
- Sung Tae, what was that?
- My joint.

1157
00:41:24,457 --> 00:41:26,967
Please choose the colour you want and write it.

1158
00:41:26,967 --> 00:41:28,367
- I can choose what I want, right?
- Yes.

1159
00:41:28,367 --> 00:41:29,567
- Here?
- You can change pens halfway too.

1160
00:41:29,567 --> 00:41:31,267
Write your name with this.

1161
00:41:31,297 --> 00:41:33,407
He's using a good colour too.

1162
00:41:33,967 --> 00:41:36,007
- That yellow colour.
- Yes.

1163
00:41:36,877 --> 00:41:37,877
(He changes to a different colour!)

1164
00:41:37,877 --> 00:41:39,247
- You can do that?
- Can I write it horizontally?

1165
00:41:39,247 --> 00:41:40,407
Yes, it doesn't matter.

1166
00:41:40,407 --> 00:41:43,617
- Only the colour matters to me.
- You're using a strong colour.

1167
00:41:44,177 --> 00:41:45,747
(She shakes the bells once again to tell Sung Tae's fortune.)

1168
00:41:45,747 --> 00:41:48,547
Is she real or not? I can't tell.

1169
00:41:55,427 --> 00:41:57,297
If she's fake, she's a very good actress.

1170
00:41:57,857 --> 00:41:59,797
(What message did she get this time?)

1171
00:41:59,997 --> 00:42:00,997
By any chance...

1172
00:42:00,997 --> 00:42:04,167
(By any chance...)

1173
00:42:04,167 --> 00:42:06,767
- Did you choose your own outfit?
- No.

1174
00:42:07,107 --> 00:42:08,237
- Did someone pick it for you?
- Yes.

1175
00:42:08,237 --> 00:42:09,937
Continue to wear like this.

1176
00:42:10,207 --> 00:42:11,437
Wear a lot of white.

1177
00:42:11,607 --> 00:42:13,247
- White really suits you.
- White?

1178
00:42:13,247 --> 00:42:14,247
- Yes.
- Okay.

1179
00:42:14,247 --> 00:42:15,277
Do you know why?

1180
00:42:15,917 --> 00:42:17,077
I don't know.

1181
00:42:17,077 --> 00:42:19,087
You have weak yellow energy.

1182
00:42:19,087 --> 00:42:20,417
(Wealth and honour)

1183
00:42:20,417 --> 00:42:23,157
You need to be bold,

1184
00:42:23,157 --> 00:42:25,257
but your personality is...

1185
00:42:25,257 --> 00:42:27,227
- Petty.
- You're timid.

1186
00:42:27,387 --> 00:42:29,997
You have so much talent...

1187
00:42:29,997 --> 00:42:32,567
- That's right.
- and so many things to show.

1188
00:42:32,567 --> 00:42:35,397
"Can I do this?" You're too shy.

1189
00:42:35,497 --> 00:42:37,737
- That's the vibe I get.
- Sung Tae is very shy.

1190
00:42:37,737 --> 00:42:40,507
So it'd be good if you stop being so shy...

1191
00:42:40,507 --> 00:42:43,337
and become braver.

1192
00:42:43,337 --> 00:42:45,577
That's what I think.

1193
00:42:46,147 --> 00:42:50,147
But as for your health...

1194
00:42:50,147 --> 00:42:51,877
It's trembling.

1195
00:42:51,877 --> 00:42:54,017
Your red energy is trembling a bit.

1196
00:42:54,017 --> 00:42:56,987
Beware of nervous tremors...

1197
00:42:57,517 --> 00:42:58,517
in the future.

1198
00:42:59,427 --> 00:43:00,527
Why?

1199
00:43:01,257 --> 00:43:02,597
Would my manager tell her stuff like this too?

1200
00:43:02,597 --> 00:43:03,897
This is so fascinating.

1201
00:43:03,897 --> 00:43:04,897
Why?

1202
00:43:04,897 --> 00:43:06,467
(What is so fascinating?)

1203
00:43:06,467 --> 00:43:08,767
This part has been twitching for one whole month.

1204
00:43:08,767 --> 00:43:10,537
- Really?
- I've been taking medicine.

1205
00:43:10,797 --> 00:43:11,837
Really?

1206
00:43:11,837 --> 00:43:12,967
(Really?)

1207
00:43:13,267 --> 00:43:14,737
That's just what I see. It's trembling.

1208
00:43:14,737 --> 00:43:16,337
Your red energy is trembling.

1209
00:43:16,337 --> 00:43:18,077
I'm serious. It was twitching this morning too.

1210
00:43:18,507 --> 00:43:19,647
This is amazing.

1211
00:43:20,047 --> 00:43:21,277
It was fascinating how she got my moving right too.

1212
00:43:21,277 --> 00:43:22,947
I moved to the southwest.

1213
00:43:22,947 --> 00:43:23,977
(He still hasn't recovered from his fortune telling.)

1214
00:43:23,977 --> 00:43:26,147
- Take magnesium.
- It didn't help,

1215
00:43:26,147 --> 00:43:27,687
so I did an MRI scan and all.

1216
00:43:28,287 --> 00:43:29,417
I did a brain scan.

1217
00:43:29,417 --> 00:43:30,557
(How did she get this right?)

1218
00:43:30,557 --> 00:43:31,557
How?

1219
00:43:31,957 --> 00:43:34,857
His manager wouldn't share his illness, right?

1220
00:43:34,987 --> 00:43:36,027
The manager...

1221
00:43:36,097 --> 00:43:37,857
They normally don't share stuff like that.

1222
00:43:37,857 --> 00:43:40,167
They wouldn't share even if they knew.

1223
00:43:40,367 --> 00:43:41,597
I'm scared.

1224
00:43:44,067 --> 00:43:47,437
(Is she a real shaman who serves Scholar Spirit?)

1225
00:43:48,737 --> 00:43:53,047
(Or is she a fake prepared by the production crew?)

1226
00:43:54,007 --> 00:43:55,677
(Thinking)

1227
00:43:55,677 --> 00:43:58,147
There are two, right?

1228
00:43:58,817 --> 00:43:59,917
Sorry?

1229
00:44:00,287 --> 00:44:03,517
It says you're torn between two scripts.

1230
00:44:03,717 --> 00:44:04,787
Yes.

1231
00:44:06,587 --> 00:44:07,727
(Surprised)

1232
00:44:08,257 --> 00:44:10,397
(For real?)

1233
00:44:10,397 --> 00:44:12,927
(Amazed)

1234
00:44:12,927 --> 00:44:15,067
This wasn't even made public.

1235
00:44:15,067 --> 00:44:17,637
But from what I can see, you'll have better energy in 2028.

1236
00:44:17,937 --> 00:44:22,937
In 2028, you'll get 2 scripts.

1237
00:44:24,277 --> 00:44:27,747
- So do I just slack off in 2027?
- In 2027...

1238
00:44:28,277 --> 00:44:31,447
(It is her personal opinion, scientifically unproven.)

1239
00:44:31,617 --> 00:44:34,947
I think the scripts you'll be getting in 2028...

1240
00:44:34,947 --> 00:44:36,157
will be much better than the scripts you'll be getting...

1241
00:44:36,157 --> 00:44:37,317
- in the near future.
- I understand.

1242
00:44:37,317 --> 00:44:39,227
Why are your palms so sweaty?

1243
00:44:40,457 --> 00:44:42,827
- I touched his palm, - Goodness.

1244
00:44:42,827 --> 00:44:44,927
and it's so wet and watery.

1245
00:44:44,927 --> 00:44:46,067
He's that nervous?

1246
00:44:46,067 --> 00:44:47,127
(He's actually very nervous.)

1247
00:44:47,127 --> 00:44:48,197
This is crazy.

1248
00:44:48,197 --> 00:44:49,937
- I want to get checked too.
- Me too.

1249
00:44:52,337 --> 00:44:55,207
She's using a white talisman because white is good for him.

1250
00:44:55,207 --> 00:44:56,277
You're right.

1251
00:44:56,937 --> 00:45:01,407
(White and blue like Sung Tae's shirt, which she said was good)

1252
00:45:01,877 --> 00:45:04,447
She used a yellow one for me because it's good for me.

1253
00:45:04,547 --> 00:45:05,947
- She's detailed.
- Exactly.

1254
00:45:06,087 --> 00:45:07,317
Even this is different.

1255
00:45:07,887 --> 00:45:09,657
- Please keep it well.
- It's white.

1256
00:45:09,817 --> 00:45:11,917
Thank you.

1257
00:45:11,917 --> 00:45:13,627
(Thank you for reading Sung Tae's fortune.)

1258
00:45:13,787 --> 00:45:16,457
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1259
00:45:17,227 --> 00:45:20,197
- Her skirt has a lot of ink stains.
- Ink stains.

1260
00:45:20,197 --> 00:45:22,097
I saw that first thing when I arrived.

1261
00:45:22,097 --> 00:45:23,537
- All the details.
- Exactly.

1262
00:45:23,537 --> 00:45:24,697
- I think she's real.
- This...

1263
00:45:24,697 --> 00:45:26,437
But I also think...

1264
00:45:26,867 --> 00:45:28,537
The way she shakes the bells...

1265
00:45:28,537 --> 00:45:30,477
looks like she's acting.

1266
00:45:30,677 --> 00:45:31,737
Exactly.

1267
00:45:31,737 --> 00:45:33,547
Don't you think so?

1268
00:45:33,777 --> 00:45:37,077
(Does it look like she's acting?)

1269
00:45:37,277 --> 00:45:38,917
I was surprised by this.

1270
00:45:38,917 --> 00:45:41,117
